& lang.toLowerCase()` change in `localeToLCID` returns the same results as before for every falsy input.\n- Replacing the module-level `sharp` with the local `sharpLib` and passing it to `decodeHeicToSharp` is behavior-neutral, and that function isn't exported.\n- `unit.sh` rebuilds before Jest, so a stale `.js` can't satisfy the oracle.\n- The Dockerfile build step should work: the image has Node 24, and `COPY server/ /server` brings in `ts-strip.js` and the root `package.json`.\n\n**Problems**\n1. **`DocService/sources/utilsDocService.js` is still tracked in git.** `git ls-files` lists it, and the diff modifies it into the emitted output (blank-padded type positions, a \"Generated…\" footer).\n   - Decision 1 says the emitted `.js` is \"not committed\". The interop doc's own pitfall says to run `git rm --cached <file>.js` when migrating, and the executor didn't. The `.gitignore` line therefore has no effect.\n   - The `.ts` and `.js` are both under version control and can drift. Every `npm run build:ts` or oracle run dirties a tracked file.\n   - The packet said to `git mv` the file, which would have removed it from the index. The `.js` is in `target.files`, so deleting it from tracking was within scope.\n2. **The `npm-shrinkwrap.json` entry for `typescript` was written by hand.** It has no `integrity` and no `requires`; the doc admits this. TypeScript 7 is a native compiler, so it likely ships per-platform optional binary packages (I couldn't check the registry). If it does, a hand-written entry can make `npm ci` fail or install a `tsc` with no binary. The pinned lock is part of the deliverable and wasn't produced by npm. `@types/node` was added to `package.json` but I saw no matching shrinkwrap change.\n3. **No follow-up packet was spawned for `.ts` linting.** The \"Spawned packets\" section is empty and no such packet exists in `.theseus/queue`. The packet required one, since `**/*.ts` is now ignored by ESLint.\n\n**To fix**\n- Run `git rm --cached DocService/sources/utilsDocService.js`, so only the `.ts` is committed and the `.gitignore` line takes effect.\n- Regenerate `npm-shrinkwrap.json` with real `npm install`, so it includes `integrity` and any platform optional dependencies, or show that the hand-written entry passes `npm ci`.\n- Spawn the `.ts` lint packet with `theseus packet new`, and record its id under \"Spawned packets\".\n\nVERDICT: REJECT Untrack the generated utilsDocService.js (git rm --cached); regenerate npm-shrinkwrap.json via real npm install instead of a hand-written typescript entry; spawn the required .ts lint follow-up packet and record it.","ttft_ms":4874,"type":"result","duration_ms":53825,"uuid":"8a0af222-84c6-4cff-8dd8-60ebb50a78ae","ttft_stream_ms":4093,"time_to_request_ms":469,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":6,"system_prompt":249,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":19,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":97,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":4,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":7,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":11,"query_setup":4,"auto_mode_context_wait":16,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":23,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":9},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":45,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":307,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":215,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":139,"process_rss_mib_result":230,"process_anon_mib_result":138,"process_peak_rss_mib":247,"process_cpu_ms_turn":1995,"process_wall_ms_turn":53824,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":795,"process_wall_ms_streaming":32794,"main_stream_count":11,"main_stream_event_count":627,"main_stream_chunk_count":108,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":7,"cpu_ms":22,"major_faults":0,"setup_ms":0,"prompt_producers_ms":0,"ambient_start_ms":8,"ambient_wait_ms":7,"render_ms":1,"p